>Quick question:  I want to set the options 'number_pad'
>'rest_on_space' and 'showexp' when I start the game up without
>re-typing them each time, and can't understand what the docs mean when
>they mention the 'NETHACKOPTIONS' command/file/line/whatever.  Any
>help out there?

This depends on wether you're playing on UNIX or MSDOS (or any other
system that I don't play on myself)...

On UNIX, you need a file called .nethackrc in your home directory. On
MSDOS, you'll need a file called NETHACK.CNF in your nethack
subdirectory. This file will be read at startup. It's possible that
nethack will scan your environment variables as well, looking for an
environmentvariable called "NETHACKOPTIONS" (UNIX again), but I`m not
sure about that. Anyway, my .nethackrc on this system contains the
following:

OPTIONS=name:Kroisos-P,safe_pet,fruit:Mandarijntje,msghistory:30,scores:2around/3top,number_pad,showexp,nosilent,nosound,time,verbose,lit_corridor,showscore

Hope this helps...

